  "caption": "Quinn joined a yoga class, and ten planks later the wrists had left the chat.\n\nWrist pain in planks and down dog is often a preparation gap rather than a sign the pose is bad. Wrists may simply not be used to carrying body weight for long, and that capacity is trainable.\n\nWhat often helps: spreading load through the whole hand with fingers wide, turning the hands out slightly, swapping to fists, handles or forearms, or using a wedge, about ten minutes of wrist training twice a week, and building weight-bearing time gradually like any other load.\n\nPain after a fall onto the hand, pins and needles, a lump, thumb-side pain with gripping, or no improvement in a few weeks is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
